---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Services" description="Funding pipeline, proposal, and program operations support for nonprofits and public-sector organizations.">
  <section class="py-20 bg-gradient-to-b from-white to-fog">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="text-5xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mb-6">Funding & Program Operations</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600">
        Two focused ways to move from opportunity to an organized, accountable scope of work.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 space-y-12">
      <div>
        <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-ridge-blue">Offer 1</span>
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-serif font-bold mb-4 text-ridge-blue">Nonprofit Funding Pipeline Sprint</h2>
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-4">
          A focused research and decision-making engagement for organizations that need to know where to pursue funding—and what must be strengthened before proposal work begins.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-700 space-y-2 ml-4">
          <li>Qualified funder prospects supported by current source research</li>
          <li>Fit, risk, exclusion, and evidence-gap analysis</li>
          <li>Priority ranking and a practical pursuit calendar</li>
          <li>Recommended next actions for internal decision-makers</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mt-4">
          Each sprint defines the geography, program focus, funder types, exclusions, research depth, calendar horizon, and revision cycle before work begins. It is a dated opportunity screen—not a promise of funding.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-ridge-blue">Offer 2</span>
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-serif font-bold mb-4 text-ridge-blue">Proposal & Program Operations Support</h2>
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-4">
          Bounded support for nonprofits, established government contractors, and public-sector organizations that need to qualify an opportunity, produce a compliant response, or launch and govern a funded program.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-700 space-y-2 ml-4">
          <li>Solicitation analysis, go/no-go support, compliance matrices, and proposal calendars</li>
          <li>Narrative, workplan, budget-to-scope alignment, document coordination, and production QA</li>
          <li>Implementation plans, roles and escalation maps, and deliverable or compliance calendars</li>
          <li>Stakeholder, partner, vendor, reporting, records, and closeout systems</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mt-4">
          Proposal development, production, subject-matter work, implementation, and ongoing operations are separated in the statement of work so ownership and approvals remain clear.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 bg-fog">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-serif font-bold mb-8 text-center">Every Engagement Has Boundaries</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 text-center mb-8">
        Before kickoff, we document deliverables, inputs, decision-makers, dates, meetings, revision cycles, data access, acceptance, payment milestones, and change control. Expansion work proceeds only through a new or amended scope.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-serif font-bold mb-12 text-center">Where We Add Value</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
        <div class="bg-fog p-6 rounded-lg">
          <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-ridge-blue">Proposal Operations</span>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mt-3">
            We can organize the pursuit, translate requirements into a controlled workplan, coordinate inputs, strengthen narrative structure, and manage production quality.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-fog p-6 rounded-lg">
          <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-ridge-blue">Program Operations</span>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mt-3">
            We can build the administrative backbone for launch, coordination, compliance, stakeholder communication, reporting, records, and closeout.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-fog p-6 rounded-lg">
          <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-ridge-blue">Specialist Boundaries</span>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mt-3">
            Clinical, legal, engineering, cybersecurity, accounting, and other specialist judgments remain with qualified professionals. Wellridge does not present itself as a clinical provider or technical prime.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-20 bg-slate-deep text-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-4xl font-serif font-bold mb-6">Prepare a Defined Need—or a Complicated One</h2>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 mb-8">
        Use the scope-preparation checklist to capture fit, responsibilities, inputs, timing, and the decision you need to make.
      </p>
      <a
        href="/contact"
        class="inline-block px-8 py-3 bg-ridge-blue text-white rounded-md text-lg font-medium hover:bg-opacity-90 transition-colors"
      >
        Prepare a Scope
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
